{
  "timestamp": "2026-10-15T13:25:07Z",
  "title": "Remove the chapter Volunteer link field and reduce WhatsApp-only city pages to three asks",
  "type": "feature",
  "userRequest": "## Summary\n\nForming (online-group) chapter pages no longer show a volunteer button (`src/components/FormingChapterCta.astro` now leads with Join WhatsApp and See online events). The chapter `volunteerUrl` field is still threaded from `src/pages/chapters/[slug].astro` through `src/components/ChapterPage.astro` into `FormingChapterCta`, which ignores it, and the content admin shows a \"Volunteer link\" field whose hint now says it is not shown.\n\n## Key Decisions\n\n- **Decided by the user on 2026-10-13: remove the field end-to-end.** Do not repurpose it.\n\n## Implementation\n\n1. Drop `volunteerUrl` from `src/content/config.ts`, `src/data/collections.json`, the `ChapterPage` and `FormingChapterCta` props, and `joinCtas` callers in `src/lib/localPresence.ts`; update `localPresence.test.ts`.",
  "description": "Removed the unused per-chapter Volunteer link field end-to-end (content schema, admin form, chapter page props, joinCtas override). WhatsApp-only (forming) city pages such as DC and Seattle now render only the hero and one band with three buttons: Request to join WhatsApp, Subscribe to newsletter, and Volunteer or co-lead (the volunteer interest form, via the new volunteerFormHref). Events lists, callouts, write-up, sign-up band, global-community band, Connect with us and the Contact us line are gone from those pages, and the forming-chapter shared-inbox surface was retired. Isolated-component previews now load the site webfonts through a small middleware (src/middleware.ts with withSiteFonts) and show real chapter copy instead of a placeholder. Scope verdict: no project deliverables were open, so none delivered or deferred this cycle. A site-wide Harvard Alumni in Tech brand-name sweep was queued as its own plan at the user's request.",
